@startuml sequence-framework-to-plugin
title Direction 2: framework → plugin (driven via bridge controller)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Playwright\n(Node)"     as Test
participant "DashboardPage\n(POM)"      as POM
participant "page.evaluate\n(CDP bridge)" as Eval
participant "window.__pluginHostBridge" as Bridge
participant "DashboardStateStoreMock\n(implements IDashboardStateController)" as Mock
participant "NgZone"            as Zone
participant "WritableSignal\n(_widgets)" as Sig
participant "Angular CD\n(OnPush)"      as CD
participant "Dashboard view"            as View

== drive ==
Test -> POM : dashboard.setWidgets([\n  {id:'a', title:'Alpha', value:10},\n  {id:'b', title:'Beta',  value:20},\n])

POM -> Eval : page.evaluate(\n  (next) => bridge\n    .controller('dashboard')\n    .setWidgets(next),\n  widgets)
activate Eval
note right of Eval
  Args structured-cloned from Node
  to browser. The arrow function is
  shipped as source text and runs in
  the page's JS context — it does
  NOT close over Node-side variables.
end note

Eval -> Bridge : controller<IDashboardStateController>('dashboard')
activate Bridge
Bridge --> Eval : Mock instance\n(registered in mock's ctor)
deactivate Bridge

Eval -> Mock : setWidgets(next)
deactivate Eval
activate Mock

== re-enter zone ==
Mock -> Zone : run(() => …)
activate Zone
Zone -> Sig : _widgets.set(next)
activate Sig
Sig -->> CD : signal change\n(consumer marks view dirty)
deactivate Sig
deactivate Zone
deactivate Mock

== render ==
CD -> CD : ApplicationRef.tick()\n(scheduled by NgZone)
activate CD
CD -> View : re-render @for / @if /\ncomputed selectedWidget()
deactivate CD
activate View
View -->> Test : new DOM observable\nvia Playwright locators
deactivate View

== verify ==
Test -> Test : await expect(\n  dashboard.widget('a'))\n  .toContainText('Alpha: 10')

note over Mock, Zone
  Without zone.run(...) the signal
  value would update but the OnPush
  view would not tick — the test
  would see stale DOM.
end note

@enduml
